 Loading Count Data The nf-core/rnaseq pipeline was run with STAR for alignment and Salmon for quantification. We load the SummarizedExperiment object produced by the pipeline, extract the raw count matrix, and assign gene symbols as row names.  Important: Salmon returns estimated counts, which are not integers. DESeq2 requires integer counts, so we round (not truncate) before building the object. This matches the tximport convention used by nf-core/differentialabundance.  Tip: If you are unsure which assay name or rowData columns are available in your RDS, inspect them first with assayNames(count_x) and names(rowData(count_x)). count_x &lt;- readRDS( file.path(git_root, &quot;data&quot;, &quot;data-02-Homo_sapiens&quot;, &quot;hasapiens&quot;, &quot;star_salmon&quot;, &quot;salmon.merged.gene.SummarizedExperiment.rds&quot;) ) # Inspect what is available (uncomment to explore): # assayNames(count_x); names(rowData(count_x)) count_genes &lt;- assay(count_x, assayNames(count_x)[1]) gene_symbols &lt;- rowData(count_x)$gene_name gene_ids &lt;- rowData(count_x)$gene_id gene_symbols_saved &lt;- ifelse( !is.na(gene_symbols) &amp; nchar(gene_symbols) &gt; 0, make.unique(as.character(gene_symbols)), make.unique(as.character(gene_ids)) ) # Salmon estimates are fractional -&gt; round to nearest integer for DESeq2 count_genes &lt;- as.matrix(count_genes) mode(count_genes) &lt;- &quot;numeric&quot; # ensure numeric, not character count_genes &lt;- round(count_genes) storage.mode(count_genes) &lt;- &quot;integer&quot; rownames(count_genes) &lt;- gene_symbols_saved cat(&quot;Dimensions (genes × samples):&quot;, dim(count_genes), &quot;
&quot;) ## Dimensions (genes &lt;U+00D7&gt; samples): 25924 16 print(head(rownames(count_genes))) ## [1] &quot;A1BG&quot; &quot;A1CF&quot; &quot;A2BP1&quot; &quot;A2LD1&quot; &quot;A2M&quot; &quot;A2ML1&quot; print(colnames(count_genes)) ## [1] &quot;N052611_albuterol_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N052611_albuterol&quot; ## [3] &quot;N052611_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N052611_untreated&quot; ## [5] &quot;N061011_albuterol_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N061011_albuterol&quot; ## [7] &quot;N061011_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N061011_untreated&quot; ## [9] &quot;N080611_albuterol_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N080611_albuterol&quot; ## [11] &quot;N080611_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N080611_untreated&quot; ## [13] &quot;N61311_albuterol_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N61311_albuterol&quot; ## [15] &quot;N61311_dexamethasone&quot; &quot;N61311_untreated&quot; # Report what the gene_id / gene_name columns actually contain. # This pipeline used a RefSeq GTF with gtf_extra_attributes = gene_name, # so both are expected to be symbols (not ENSEMBL). Confirm here: cat(&quot;
Example gene_id :&quot;, paste(head(gene_ids, 3), collapse = &quot;, &quot;), &quot;
&quot;) ## ## Example gene_id : A1BG, A1CF, A2BP1 cat(&quot;Example gene_name:&quot;, paste(head(gene_symbols, 3), collapse = &quot;, &quot;), &quot;
&quot;) ## Example gene_name: A1BG, A1CF, A2BP1 cat(&quot;gene_id look like ENSEMBL? :&quot;, any(grepl(&quot;^ENSG&quot;, head(gene_ids, 50))), &quot;
&quot;) ## gene_id look like ENSEMBL? : FALSE  Note: This dataset was processed against a RefSeq GRCh37 GTF with gtf_extra_attributes = gene_name, so both gene_id and gene_name hold gene symbols (e.g. A1BG), not ENSEMBL IDs. Symbols are exactly what g:Profiler and MSigDB accept, so no ID conversion is needed downstream. The check above prints the actual values so you can confirm this on your own RDS. # Persist gene_id &lt;-&gt; gene_name map for downstream scripts id_map &lt;- data.frame( gene_id = as.character(gene_ids), gene_symbol = gene_symbols_saved, stringsAsFactors = FALSE ) dir.create(file.path(git_root, &quot;results&quot;, &quot;human&quot;), recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE) saveRDS(id_map, file.path(git_root, &quot;results&quot;, &quot;human&quot;, &quot;gene_id_symbol_map.rds&quot;))

